4. Authentication and authorization
Goal
Allow users to manage their own account and listings without being able to modify another user's resources.
Authentication
Passwords are hashed using bcrypt.
Login creates a signed JSON Web Token.
The token is stored in an HTTP-only cookie.
Protected requests use the authentication cookie.
/api/auth/me returns the currently authenticated user.
Authorization
Only authenticated users can create listings.
Only the listing owner can update or delete a listing.
Only the authenticated profile owner can update or delete their profile.
sellerId is assigned by the backend using the authenticated user ID.

5. Validation and basic security
The MVP includes basic security suitable for a hobby project:
Zod request validation
bcrypt password hashing
JWT authentication
HTTP-only authentication cookies
protected routes
ownership checks
Helmet security headers
rate limiting for registration and login
restricted CORS configuration
frontend display of backend validation errors
server-side control of listing ownership
Advanced production security is outside the current MVP scope.

6. Frontend and backend connection
